# pgai-agent-kanban: crontab-large.example
#
# Hardware assumption: 8+ cores / 16+ GB RAM, dedicated high-throughput host.
#
# Tier: large
# Design choice: three separate tier files (small/medium/large) rather than a
#   parameterized template.  Each file is self-contained and flows through the
#   existing __KANBAN_ROOT__ / __CLAUDE_PATH__ substitution and
#   safe_overwrite_crontab mechanism in install-crontab.sh unchanged.
#   Install with: team/scripts/install-crontab.sh  (after pointing it at this
#   file, or by substituting manually as shown below).
#
# Cadence: every minute, pipeline-ordered with sub-minute stagger.
#   Agents fire in pipeline order within each minute:
#     :00+00s  PM      (plans; leads the minute)
#     :00+12s  CODER   (produces code)
#     :00+24s  WRITER  (produces docs)
#     :00+36s  TESTER  (verifies what the producers finished)
#     :00+48s  CM      (releases; last, so it sees the TESTER's result)
#
#   PM leads, the two producers follow, then the two consumers in the order
#   the pipeline hands work along: TESTER before CM, so a verification that
#   finishes in a minute is read by the release step in that same minute
#   instead of waiting for the next one. Any handoff therefore lands in the
#   same minute or the next.
#
# Maximum agent-to-agent handoff latency: ~60 seconds (one full minute cycle).
# Best-case handoff (adjacent pipeline slot): 12-24 seconds.
# Recommended for: 8+ core dedicated servers, high-throughput CI machines,
#   production kanban instances requiring minimum RC latency.
#
# IMPORTANT: Replace __KANBAN_ROOT__ and __CLAUDE_PATH__ with real values
# before installing.  install-crontab.sh performs these substitutions
# automatically.
#
# Manual install:
#   sed -e "s|__KANBAN_ROOT__|/your/kanban/root|g" \
#       -e "s|__CLAUDE_PATH__|/usr/local/bin|g" \
#     team/templates/install/crontab-large.example | crontab -

# --- Environment ---
# PGAI_AGENT_KANBAN_ROOT_PATH — the kanban root every job below acts on,
#   exported to each job. No default: install-crontab.sh writes the
#   installed root on the line below. Because it is exported,
#   entry points other than the wake (overwatch-sweep.sh, cleanup.sh) do not
#   source shell-env or claude-env: anything they need must be on the PATH
#   line below.
# PATH — cron's own PATH is minimal. This one must reach the claude CLI, a
#   python3 of version 3.12+, and the codex CLI when that provider is
#   active. Default: the directory holding `claude` when install-crontab.sh
#   runs (/usr/local/bin when claude is not on its PATH), followed by
#   /usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin.
PGAI_AGENT_KANBAN_ROOT_PATH=__KANBAN_ROOT__
PATH=__CLAUDE_PATH__:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

# =============================================================================
# LARGE-TIER PATTERN — every-minute firing with sub-minute pipeline-ordered
#                      stagger across all five agents
# =============================================================================
# Fires every minute. Agents are interleaved by sub-minute sleep offset, in
# pipeline order:
#   :00+00s  PM      — planner
#   :00+12s  CODER   — producer
#   :00+24s  WRITER  — producer
#   :00+36s  TESTER  — consumer (verifies)
#   :00+48s  CM      — consumer (releases; last so it reads the TESTER's result)
#
# Operator tuning:
#   - Adjust sleep offsets (12, 24, 36, 48) for wider/narrower stagger.
#   - Use 0-59 for N in --sleep=N; values >= 60 trigger a warning.
#   - Reduce to every-2-minutes (*/2 / 1-59/2) if API rate limits are hit.

# --- Planner ---
# PM fires every minute at :00 (no sleep offset — leads the minute)
* * * * * __KANBAN_ROOT__/scripts/wake-batch.sh --agent=pm     --sleep=0  >> __KANBAN_ROOT__/logs/cron-pm.log 2>&1

# --- Producers: CODER, WRITER ---
# CODER fires every minute with 12-second delay: :00+12s
* * * * * __KANBAN_ROOT__/scripts/wake-batch.sh --agent=coder  --sleep=12 >> __KANBAN_ROOT__/logs/cron-coder.log 2>&1

# WRITER fires every minute with 24-second delay: :00+24s
* * * * * __KANBAN_ROOT__/scripts/wake-batch.sh --agent=writer --sleep=24 >> __KANBAN_ROOT__/logs/cron-writer.log 2>&1

# --- Consumers: TESTER, then CM ---
# TESTER fires every minute with 36-second delay: :00+36s
* * * * * __KANBAN_ROOT__/scripts/wake-batch.sh --agent=tester --sleep=36 >> __KANBAN_ROOT__/logs/cron-tester.log 2>&1

# CM fires every minute with 48-second delay (last, reads the TESTER's result): :00+48s
* * * * * __KANBAN_ROOT__/scripts/wake-batch.sh --agent=cm     --sleep=48 >> __KANBAN_ROOT__/logs/cron-cm.log 2>&1

# --- Cleanup Script (weekly, Sundays at 4:00 AM) ---
# With no --project, cleanup.sh runs once per project registered in
# projects.cfg (one result line per project in the log). Add
# --project <name> to clean a single project instead.
0 4 * * 0 __KANBAN_ROOT__/scripts/cleanup/cleanup.sh >> __KANBAN_ROOT__/logs/cron-cleanup.log 2>&1

# --- Trivial-log purge (daily at 04:15, opt-in) ---
# Uncomment to enable daily purge of small stale batch logs. Like the
# weekly line above it needs no --project; the purge is framework-wide.
# 15 4 * * * __KANBAN_ROOT__/scripts/cleanup/cleanup.sh --trivial-only >> __KANBAN_ROOT__/logs/cron-cleanup-trivial.log 2>&1

# --- Weekly coverage run (Sundays at 05:00, opt-in) ---
# The operator's weekly coverage run of the unit suite (PGAI_TESTING_COVERAGE=1 lets --coverage collect while kanban.cfg [testing] coverage stays false); to enable, replace /path/to/dev-tree with your dev tree checkout and uncomment:
# 0 5 * * 0 PGAI_TESTING_COVERAGE=1 /path/to/dev-tree/team/scripts/run-unit-tests.sh --coverage >> __KANBAN_ROOT__/logs/cron-coverage.log 2>&1

# --- OVERWATCH Tier-1 sweep (hourly at :30) ---
# Fires once per hour at minute 30.  In the large tier, every minute is
# occupied by at least two agent wake lines, so exact separation is impossible.
# Minute 30 is the conventional overwatch slot — it fires hourly (not every
# minute) so real contention with agent wakes is bounded and brief.
# Operator tuning: adjust the minute (30) to any preferred slot. To widen the
# sweep interval, change the second field from * to */2 (every-2-hours), etc.
30 * * * * __KANBAN_ROOT__/scripts/overwatch-sweep.sh >> __KANBAN_ROOT__/logs/cron-overwatch-sweep.log 2>&1

# --- Log Cleanup (daily at 04:30) ---
30 4 * * * __KANBAN_ROOT__/scripts/cleanup/cleanup_logs.sh >> __KANBAN_ROOT__/logs/cron-cleanup-logs.log 2>&1
